// loft#2391 — A CALL HANDED A VIEW AND A CONTAINER IT OVERWRITES IS REFUSED (`@FR-B-Ref-Reshape`, `@FR-B-Disturb`).  A plain parameter aliases the caller's value (`calls.md` F-ParamHeap), so `put(c, y)` with `y` unwrapped out of `c.tp` and `put` writing `c.tp = y` hands the callee a reference into the record its own write releases.
//
// @falsified-at: f6ee9b1a9 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// HOLDS: the same write inline materialises the view instead —
//   `rules/binding/B-Disturb/2391-a-whole-record-written-into-a-place-ends-the-views-into-what-it-owned.loft` (a2).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot pass both `c` and a reference into it to `put`

enum Ty { Opt { inner: Ty }, Int { bits: integer } }
struct Cell { tp: Ty }

fn put(c: Cell, y: Ty) { c.tp = y; }

fn main() {
  c = Cell { tp: Opt { inner: Int { bits: 32 } } };
  y = match c.tp { Opt { inner } => inner, _ => c.tp };
  put(c, y);
  println("{match c.tp { Int { bits } => bits, _ => -1 }}");
}
